{XPPMATH 20 "6#>%$eq8G/-%%I_COG6#%$RMSG,$*&*(&%\"VG6#%$OUTG\"\"\",&&F.
6#%#INGF1F-!\"\"F1-%%sqrtG6#\"\"$\"\"\"F;*(F3\"\"\"&%\"LGF/\"\"\"&%\"f
G6#%#SWG\"\"\"!\"\"#F1\"\"'" }}}}{SECT 0 {PARA 3 "" 0 "" {TEXT -1 6 "I
nputs" }}{EXCHG {PARA 0 "> " 0 "" {MPLTEXT 1 0 1842 "#################
##############\n# 5.05V\n################################\n\nV[OUT(TAR
GET)] := 5.05;\n\n# Maximum output current for 5.05V is ~1.7A:\n#   25
0ma baseline\n#   900ma USB 1.1\n#   200ma for PMOD\n#   350ma buffer
\n# But we set the TPS54624x max of 4A to be safe.\nI_OUT := 4;\n\n# F
or 5V, we prefer parallel resistors of similar values to statistically
\n# minimize error due to the 1% tolerance. \nR1[ACTUAL] := evalf(R_Pa
rallel(120*k, 220*k));\nR2[ACTUAL] := evalf(R_Parallel(20*k, 22*k));\n
\n# Derate capacitors for 5.05V\nC_4u7 := 4.7 * (1 - 0.6644926) * u; #
 https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL05A475MP5NRN.do\nC_10u :=  10 *
 (1 - 0.5385295) * u; # https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL10A106MA
8NRN.do\nC_22u :=  22 * (1 - 0.5230603) * u; # https://product.samsung
sem.com/mlcc/CL21A226MAQNNN.do\n\n################################\n# \+
6.1V\n################################\n\nV[OUT(TARGET)] := 6.1;\n\n# \+
Maximum output current for 6.1V is ~1.2A:\n#   400ma - Datasette A (bl
ack C2N stalled at end-of-tape rewind)\n#   400ma - Datasette B (\")\n
#   400ma - Buffer\n# But we set the TPS54624x max of 4A to be safe.\n
I_OUT := 4;\n\n# For 6V the voltage is less critical, so we just use a
vailable 0402 1% resistors.\n\nR1[ACTUAL] := 120*k;\nR2[ACTUAL] := 13*
k;\n\n# Derate capacitors for 6.1V\nC_4u7 := 4.7 * (1 - 0.7272049) * u
; # https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL05A475MP5NRN.do\nC_10u :=  1
0 * (1 - 0.6176601) * u; # https://product.samsungsem.com/mlcc/CL10A10
6MA8NRN.do\nC_22u :=  22 * (1 - 0.6025791) * u; # https://product.sams
ungsem.com/mlcc/CL21A226MAQNNN.do\n\n################################
\n# Common\n################################\n\nL[ACTUAL] := 1.8*u:\nC
[OUT(ACTUAL)] := C_22u + C_22u;\n\n# Unregulated supply is about 12V u
nloaded.  We'll use the TPS54624x max of 16V to be safe.\nV[IN(MAX)] :
= 16;\n\n# Maximum switching frequency is 1.2 MHz\nf[SW] := 1.2*M;" }}
